{"id": "EUVD-2026-93123", "enisaUuid": "45738c7e-7153-3eeb-9f2a-045d4ab30a1d", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: iwlegacy: fix broadcast stations deallocation\n\nOn the error path of __il4965_up(), il_dealloc_bcast_stations() clears\nonly IL_STA_UCODE_ACTIVE, leaving IL_STA_BCAST set. This causes the\nsame broadcast stations to be deallocated again by __il4965_down().\n\nThis can occur when RF_KILL is toggled during driver startup.\n\nTo fix clear the entire 'used' field, since we will not do any\nother operations on the station.", "datePublished": "2026-10-06T08:44:34", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:15:26", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/275d474a4b4bd4e73b18b1452f12e78806a8843a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/526fdd45548e22eee50ee1062abd88269d9f32e0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c9a116d691364cd7f59d8329b395adcaf826d5c6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/85d847ff71fe736cbc15ada321256818e630e205", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1d84c2a3de449aceb94ed79eaefecdf1bedb6468", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/55d34422c0d91436983028fd3c1546a1c2bee55f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a9176fe666af1730cab92350f9c8cf67ebf14439", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b5526b780f8b297a76030410b96ba29153afb98f"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98195", "GHSA-9fj7-g454-67r4"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "00d07e86-371d-3d98-a588-7dce3b86ac1d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.8"}, {"id": "041e017d-01fd-306e-9277-5f7b9bc6ba65", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "0e6651f6-f9cf-31a9-b318-6aff9d3fda94", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c2fd34469d1623111e3c3db65cde533f3bddc26e <526fdd45548e22eee50ee1062abd88269d9f32e0"}, {"id": "1c9f49fa-3d9d-3a82-bcbc-63eb4385eda5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "